<section class="blk">
  <div class="eyebrow">Section 1</div>
  <h2 class="rv">What <span class="gt">Lawha</span> is</h2>
  <p class="rv">Lawha is a visual work management platform. Work is modelled as a hierarchy anyone
  understands on sight — boards hold lists, lists hold cards — and everything else in the product
  exists to create, route, schedule, group or report on those cards.</p>
  <p class="rv">The design bet is simplicity plus automation. A team should be productive in the
  first five minutes and still be able to encode a real process by month three, without the board
  ever becoming something only its author can read. Arabic and English are both first-class:
  right-to-left layout, bilingual search, and AI that works natively in either.</p>
  <p class="rv"><strong>In scope:</strong> all end-user, administrative, automation, AI, integration,
  platform and developer capabilities. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> commercial packaging,
  go-to-market, and infrastructure implementation detail.</p>
  <div class="note rv">Every module carries two visuals: an original schematic showing how the
  concept is structured, and an interface concept showing what the module looks like in use. Both
  are drawn as vector art from the requirements themselves — they are design intent, not a built
  product. The working UI comes next, once this specification is signed off.</div>
</section>

