  <div class="tw rv"><table class=""><thead><tr><th class="c-term">Term</th><th class="c-def">Definition</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c-term">Organisation</td><td class="c-def">Top-level container grouping multiple workspaces under one policy and identity entity.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-term">Workspace</td><td class="c-def">A team container holding boards, members, settings and shared views.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-term">Board</td><td class="c-def">A single project or workflow surface containing lists.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-term">List</td><td class="c-def">A vertical column on a board, typically a workflow stage.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-term">Card</td><td class="c-def">The atomic unit of work, holding all task detail.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-term">Extension</td><td class="c-def">An installable module that adds capability to a board without changing the core.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-term">Lawha Flow</td><td class="c-def">The native no-code automation engine.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-term">Lawha AI</td><td class="c-def">The intelligence layer that reads and writes board content on the user&#x27;s behalf.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-term">Inbox</td><td class="c-def">A personal capture queue for items not yet assigned to a board.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-term">Planner</td><td class="c-def">A personal calendar surface for time-blocking cards.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-term">MCP</td><td class="c-def">Model Context Protocol, the open standard letting external AI assistants read and write Lawha data.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</section>

