<section class="blk">
  <div class="eyebrow">Section 7</div><h2 class="rv">Non-functional requirements</h2>
  <div class="tw rv"><table class=""><thead><tr><th class="c-id">ID</th><th class="c-req">Category</th><th class="c-def">Requirement</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c-id">NFR-01</td><td class="c-req">Usability</td><td class="c-def">A first-time user must create a board and card without training or documentation.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">NFR-02</td><td class="c-req">Performance</td><td class="c-def">Board load and card drag must feel instantaneous at typical board sizes.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">NFR-03</td><td class="c-req">Scalability</td><td class="c-def">Tens of millions of concurrent boards without per-tenant degradation.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">NFR-04</td><td class="c-req">Availability</td><td class="c-def">High availability with a contractual service level agreement for organisation accounts.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">NFR-05</td><td class="c-req">Consistency</td><td class="c-def">Real-time state convergence across web, desktop and mobile clients.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">NFR-06</td><td class="c-req">Security</td><td class="c-def">Encryption in transit and at rest with enterprise identity federation.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">NFR-07</td><td class="c-req">Extensibility</td><td class="c-def">The core stays lean; depth is delivered through the Extension ecosystem.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">NFR-08</td><td class="c-req">Interoperability</td><td class="c-def">Open REST API, webhooks and MCP for bi-directional integration.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">NFR-09</td><td class="c-req">Data portability</td><td class="c-def">Users must be able to export their data in open formats.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">NFR-10</td><td class="c-req">AI governance</td><td class="c-def">AI must be admin-toggleable and must not alter user data without explicit confirmation.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <div class="eyebrow">Section 8</div>
  <h2 class="rv">Assumptions, constraints and dependencies</h2>
  <p class="rv"><strong>Assumptions.</strong> Teams organise work visually in stages suited to a
  Kanban model, and a meaningful share of users will work primarily in Arabic.</p>
  <p class="rv"><strong>Constraints.</strong> Cloud-delivered multi-tenant service. Native reporting
  is intentionally shallow — three chart families, with anything deeper handled through export or the
  API. There is no native time tracking, resource levelling or budgeting, and no hard dependency
  model between cards; sequencing is expressed through dates and links.</p>
  <p class="rv"><strong>Dependencies.</strong> A hosted language model for the intelligence layer, an
  identity provider for federated access, and third-party extension authors for capability beyond
  the core.</p>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <div class="eyebrow">Section 9</div><h2 class="rv">Gaps and risks</h2>
  <div class="tw rv"><table class=""><thead><tr><th class="c-id">ID</th><th class="c-req">Gap or risk</th><th class="c-def">Impact</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c-id">R-01</td><td class="c-req">Simplicity ceiling as teams mature</td><td class="c-def">Groups outgrow the model and migrate to heavier tooling.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">R-02</td><td class="c-req">Extension dependency for core project needs</td><td class="c-def">Fragmented experience and inconsistent quality across boards.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">R-03</td><td class="c-req">Board sprawl at scale</td><td class="c-def">Loss of visibility and ownership without organisation-level governance.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">R-04</td><td class="c-req">Limited native reporting</td><td class="c-def">Programme sponsors need external business-intelligence tooling.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">R-05</td><td class="c-req">Bilingual parity drift</td><td class="c-def">Arabic experience degrades to a translation layer rather than a first-class interface.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">R-06</td><td class="c-req">AI trust and reversibility</td><td class="c-def">Users disable AI entirely if a generative action cannot be cleanly undone.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">R-07</td><td class="c-req">Real-time sync under load</td><td class="c-def">Concurrent editing conflicts erode confidence in the board as a source of truth.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">R-08</td><td class="c-req">Notification fatigue</td><td class="c-def">Over-notification trains users to ignore the product.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <div class="eyebrow">Section 10</div><h2 class="rv">Success metrics</h2>
  <div class="tw rv"><table class=""><thead><tr><th class="c-id">ID</th><th class="c-def">Metric</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c-id">SM-01</td><td class="c-def">Time from first login to first card created.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">SM-02</td><td class="c-def">Weekly active boards per workspace.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">SM-03</td><td class="c-def">Share of cards created through capture, automation or AI rather than manual entry.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">SM-04</td><td class="c-def">Automation runs executed per workspace per month.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">SM-05</td><td class="c-def">AI feature adoption and sustained reuse after first week.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">SM-06</td><td class="c-def">Manual administrative time saved per user per week.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">SM-07</td><td class="c-def">Proportion of sessions conducted in Arabic.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">SM-08</td><td class="c-def">Extension installation rate per active board.</td></tr><tr><td class="c-id">SM-09</td><td class="c-def">Median board load time at the ninety-fifth percentile.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</section>

